  "summary": "Reverse shell to hardcoded remote endpoint on require",
  "details": "The gem's library entry point unconditionally opens a TCP connection to the hardcoded remote address 66.78.40.218:32768, redirects STDIN, STDOUT, and STDERR to that socket, and execs /bin/sh -i. Any process that performs `require \"zzhelloworld_socktest\"` immediately hands interactive shell control of the installer's host to the remote endpoint, with no authentication or gating. The behavior fires on load, so simply importing the gem (including transitively) is sufficient to establish the reverse shell.",
